UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Flux is an image, video, and world-model family from Black Forest Labs. The current generation is FLUX 3 (image, video with native audio, an open-weights Action/robotics model, and the open-weights Image Klein variant), with the FLUX.2 lineup still offered alongside it.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'flux' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Flux is a family of generative AI models built by Black Forest Labs, spanning top-tier API-only models and open-weight versions you can self-host and fine-tune. It originally focused on image generation and editing, but the company has since expanded well beyond images.

The current generation is FLUX 3, announced July 23, 2026, covering FLUX 3 Image, FLUX 3 Video (which adds native audio), and FLUX 3 Action, an open-weights model aimed at robotics, released September 23, 2026. On October 15, 2026, Black Forest Labs added FLUX 3 Image Klein, a 5.6-billion-parameter open-weights model (base and distilled versions, API model id flux-3-image-klein) released under the FLUX Kommunity License. The earlier FLUX.2 lineup (pro, flex, max, dev, and the compact klein variant in 4B and 9B sizes, added January 2026) remains available, as do several legacy FLUX.1 tiers including Kontext Pro/Max and Pro Ultra.

Across the lineup, Flux models support multi-reference input (up to around 10 reference images) for character and style consistency, photorealistic image output up to 4 megapixels, and text rendering inside generated images. FLUX 3 Image Klein is built for consumer hardware: its INT8 build runs on GeForce RTX GPUs with as little as 8GB of VRAM, generating a 1-megapixel image in about 4 seconds on an RTX 5090 and under 9 seconds on an RTX 4070. FLUX 3 Video adds synchronized audio generation.

Pricing is pay-as-you-go with no subscriptions or seat fees. FLUX 3 Image is billed per image: about $0.041 at 768 square, $0.048 at 1k, $0.100 at 2k, and $0.607 at 4k. FLUX 3 Image Klein starts from $0.009 per image at 1k resolution, making it the cheapest model currently offered through Black Forest Labs' API. FLUX 3 Video is billed per second, from roughly $0.06/s for drafts up to $0.17-$0.80/s depending on quality, with continuation generations at $0.41-$0.95/s. FLUX.2 lists starting per-image prices of about $0.014 (klein 4B), $0.015 (klein 9B), $0.03 (pro), $0.05 (flex), and $0.07 (max); the vendor's own pricing calculator has shown different default figures for some of these tiers, so exact per-image costs can vary. Legacy FLUX.1 tiers run roughly $0.04-$0.08 per image. Commercial self-hosting above certain volumes requires a separate annual Open Weights license (Builder, up to 10,000 images/month; Platform; Professional, up to 100,000 images/month; Enterprise; and Synthetic Data tiers), with pricing not published on the vendor's pricing page.

There is no free hosted API tier. Free self-hosting is available for FLUX 3 Image Klein, whose weights are free for commercial use by individuals and companies with annual revenue under $5 million under the FLUX Kommunity License, and for FLUX.1 [schnell] (Apache 2.0); FLUX.1 [dev] remains non-commercial, and larger organizations need a paid self-hosting license or the API. The fast-expanding lineup, inconsistent per-image figures between docs and calculator, and license tiers for commercial self-hosting add complexity for buyers comparing options.

Flux suits developers and studios that want either top-tier image or video generation through an API, or a self-hostable, fine-tunable model, and that are comfortable with pay-per-asset billing or managing an open-weights license.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'flux' AND lang = 'en';

