UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Recraft AI is a design-focused image generator built around its Recraft V4.1 model family, including a fast Flash variant. It produces photorealistic raster images, true SVG vectors, icons, mockups and product shots from text prompts.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'recraft-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Recraft AI is an image-generation platform aimed at designers, marketers and product teams rather than casual users. It runs in a browser-based Studio where you write prompts, control style and export results as raster or editable vector files.

The current model lineup is the Recraft V4.1 family, released in May 2026: a standard V4.1 model plus Pro (2K), Vector, Pro Vector and Utility variants. On September 23, 2026, Recraft added V4.1 Flash, a separate, faster raster-only model with a median generation time of about 1.3 seconds per image and no style controls. An Exploration Mode generates several visual directions from a single prompt.

Beyond its own models, Recraft Studio integrates third-party image engines - Nano Banana, Seedream, GPT Image and Flux - available from the Basic plan up, and video models including Kling, Grok Imagine Video, Veo and Seedance, available from the Pro plan up, so you can compare outputs without switching tools.

Pricing is credit-based, and the figures below reflect annual billing, which Recraft discounts by about 20% compared to monthly. Basic costs $10/month billed annually ($120/year) for 1,000 credits per month and commercial usage rights. Pro starts at $16/month billed annually ($192/year) for 2,000 credits, with higher credit tiers available plus access to the video models. Teams costs $18/seat/month billed annually ($211/year) for 2,000 credits per seat, a shared workspace and SSO; Enterprise plans use custom quotes. Recraft also offers pay-per-image API pricing, from about $0.007 per image on V4.1 Flash up to $0.30 per image on Pro Vector. Top-up credit packs of 200 to 1,600 credits do not expire.

The free plan is restricted rather than a genuine alternative to paying: it offers limited free credits, capped at three generations per style per day, three uploads per day and up to two images per generation, using only Recraft's own models with no parallel generation. Images made on the free plan are public, owned by Recraft, and carry no commercial license, so serious use requires a paid plan. Heavy raster or upscaling work can also burn through credits quickly on the entry-level tiers.

Recraft suits teams that need both clean vectors and realistic raster from one platform, and value consistent style control. It is less suited to hobbyists who just want free, unrestricted images.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'recraft-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET pros = ARRAY[$x$Produces genuine editable SVG vectors alongside photorealistic raster, which few competitors do well$x$, $x$The V4.1 family, plus the fast new V4.1 Flash variant, extends the tool well beyond icons into mockups, product shots and utility imagery$x$, $x$Studio bundles third-party image models (Nano Banana, Seedream, GPT Image, Flux) and video models (Kling, Grok Imagine Video, Veo, Seedance) in one place$x$, $x$Strong, consistent style controls that keep brand looks coherent across a set of assets$x$, $x$Top-up credit packs never expire, so occasional users are not forced into a subscription$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'recraft-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET cons = ARRAY[$x$Free tier is capped (three generations per style per day, Recraft's own models only) and generated images are public, owned by Recraft, with no commercial license$x$, $x$Credit-based pricing can get expensive fast for high-volume raster, vector or upscaling work$x$, $x$Steeper learning curve than one-click generators; it is built for designers, not casual users$x$, $x$Commercial rights and privacy only unlock on a paid plan, starting at $10/month billed annually$x$, $x$Quality of integrated third-party models varies, and they consume credits like native generations$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'recraft-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET choose_if = $x$["You need both editable SVG vectors and photorealistic raster from a single tool", "You want brand-consistent icons, mockups and product shots at scale", "You value trying multiple image and video models inside one Studio", "You are on a paid plan and require clear commercial licensing", "You produce assets regularly and can justify a credit subscription"]$x$::jsonb
 WHERE slug = 'recraft-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET faq = $x$[{"q": "What is Recraft AI?", "a": "Recraft AI is an AI image generator specialized in vector graphics and brand-consistent design. Unlike most AI tools that produce raster images, Recraft can generate true SVG vector files, icon sets, and scalable brand assets. It's popular with designers who need production-ready design files."}, {"q": "Can Recraft AI generate SVG files?", "a": "Yes. This is Recraft's primary differentiator — it generates true SVG (scalable vector graphics) files that can be scaled to any size without quality loss. This makes it essential for logo design, icon creation, and any print or large-format design work."}, {"q": "Is Recraft AI free?", "a": "Recraft's free plan offers limited free credits: three generations per style per day, three uploads per day, up to two images per generation, and Recraft's own models only. Free-plan images are public, owned by Recraft, and not licensed for commercial use. Paid plans start at $10/month billed annually for Basic (1,000 credits/month with commercial rights), with Pro starting at $16/month billed annually for 2,000 credits, plus Teams and custom Enterprise options."}, {"q": "What is the difference between Recraft and Midjourney for design work?", "a": "Recraft is optimized for design assets — vectors, icons, consistent brand visuals. Midjourney is optimized for artistic image quality. Designers needing production files use Recraft; artists and creative professionals use Midjourney. Many designers use both for different purposes."}]$x$::jsonb
