UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Gamma is an AI tool for generating presentations, documents, and websites from a prompt. The current release, Gamma 5, adds a new agent that asks questions and keeps context across edits, plus a fully freeform editing canvas.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'gamma' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Gamma is a web-based tool that turns a short prompt or an outline into a finished presentation, document, or simple website. Instead of arranging slides by hand, you describe what you want and Gamma builds the structure, writing, and layout for you to refine.

The current version is Gamma 5, launched October 6, 2026, which Gamma describes as 'the biggest product overhaul in our company's history.' It rolled out to every user on every plan and replaces the earlier Gamma 3.0 release.

Gamma 5 widens the range of visual styles available and lets you switch between agent-led editing and a fully freeform canvas for arranging individual elements by hand. A new agent asks clarifying questions and keeps context across edits rather than requiring one detailed prompt upfront. The release also adds enterprise connectors, with Slack threads and Granola transcripts given as examples, and lets you import existing PowerPoint, PDF, or infographic files while preserving their original design.

Pricing is organized into Free, Plus, Pro, and Ultra individual plans, plus Business and Enterprise options. The Free plan costs $0, includes 400 credits at signup with no time limit, and requires no credit card; it allows up to 10 slides per prompt, carries Gamma branding, and can export to PDF, PPTX, PNG, and Google Slides. Plus costs $12 per seat per month billed monthly, or $9 per seat per month billed annually ($108 per year), with 1,000 monthly credits. Pro costs $25 per seat per month billed monthly, or $18 per seat per month billed annually ($216 per year), and adds API access, 4,000 monthly credits, and up to 10 custom domains. Ultra costs $100 per seat per month billed monthly, or $90 per seat per month billed annually ($1,080 per year), with 20,000 monthly credits and up to 100 custom domains. Business costs $40 per seat per month, billed annually only ($480 per year), with 10,000 monthly credits per seat, SSO, and up to 100 custom domains. Enterprise pricing is custom and adds SCIM and priority support. Annual billing saves up to 28% versus paying monthly.

Credits are consumed by AI generation, so heavy users can burn through an allowance quickly, and the Free plan's 400 credits are a fixed, one-time grant rather than a recurring monthly allowance. Free plan output carries Gamma branding until you upgrade. No separate Team plan currently appears among Gamma's listed tiers; multi-seat use falls under Business or custom Enterprise pricing.

Gamma suits people who need to produce decks, one-pagers, or landing pages fast and value speed over pixel-level control, though the new freeform canvas narrows that gap. It is a strong fit for founders, marketers, educators, and teams that want a consistent house style without a dedicated designer.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'gamma' AND lang = 'en';

