UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Semrush is a marketing and SEO platform for keyword research, competitor analysis, site audits and content optimization. In 2026 Adobe acquired Semrush and the product was repositioned around an 'SEO + AI Search' plan family that adds an AI Visibility Toolkit tracking how brands show up in ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'semrush' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Semrush is one of the longest-running online-visibility platforms, built around keyword research, rank tracking, backlink and traffic analysis, technical site audits and content tools. Marketers, agencies and SEO teams use it to size up competitors and plan campaigns across search and paid channels.

Adobe completed its acquisition of Semrush on April 28, 2026, for roughly $1.9 billion at $12 per share, and Semrush now sits inside Adobe's CX Enterprise portfolio. Around the same time the product line was reorganized into an 'SEO + AI Search' plan family covering Free, SEO, Starter, Pro+, Advanced and a custom Enterprise tier.

The current toolkit bundles the classic SEO features with an AI Visibility Toolkit that monitors brand mentions across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews, an LLM Gap Analyzer app, and Bot and Agent Analytics that show which AI crawlers are hitting your site. AI visibility depth scales by tier: Starter includes 50 prompts/day and 300 AI visibility reports/day on one domain plus MCP access, Pro+ raises that to 100 prompts/day, and Advanced offers unlimited prompts across 40+ websites with 5,000+ tracked keywords and API access.

On monthly billing the published SEO + AI Search tiers are $139/mo for SEO, $199/mo for Starter and $299/mo for Pro+; paying annually lowers these to about $117.33, $165.17 and $248.17 per month respectively, saving up to 17%. Advanced is custom-priced and requires requesting a demo, as is Enterprise. A free account (one demo project, 10 reports per day across the vital tools, no credit card) is also available, along with add-ons such as extra user seats from $45/mo, Lead Generation at $90/mo, and Base and Pro Reports at $10 and $20 per month.

The main drawbacks are cost and complexity: entry pricing is high for freelancers, the top Advanced tier has no public price and requires a sales conversation, add-ons stack up quickly, and the breadth of tools and plan names create a real learning curve. The most useful AI-visibility features sit on the Starter plan and above, not the base SEO tier.

Semrush fits agencies, in-house marketing teams and serious SEO practitioners who want one platform covering both traditional search rankings and the newer question of how a brand surfaces inside AI answers.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'semrush' AND lang = 'en';

